### Global CSS

To customize form layout and spacing, use the `className` prop on `<Form>` or add a project-level class with the `@layer components` directive.
[Learn more](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/adding-custom-styles#adding-component-classes).

`Form` renders a native `<form>` element and focuses on validation and submission. It does not include dedicated BEM classes in `@heroui/styles`—apply container styles from global CSS, and use field components for control-level customization.

```css
@layer components {
  .form-layout {
    @apply flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface p-4 shadow-sm;
  }
}
```

```tsx
<Form className="form-layout" onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
  {/* TextField, Input, Button, etc. */}
</Form>
```

For grouped fields with shared layout, use [Fieldset](./fieldset) and target `.fieldset`, `.fieldset__legend`, and related classes. For individual controls, see **Global CSS** on [TextField](./text-field), [Input](./input), [Label](./label), and [FieldError](./field-error).

